The Soundscape Theaters is a cinema on the [[Geography/Black and White/Plaza|plaza]] in the [[Geography/Black and White/index|Black and White]]. It is boarded up, with a speaker on a pole outside. Pouring a caught sound into the speaker turns it back to its working state: fresh paint, a revolving door, and a lobby with a concession stand, film posters, and a velvet rope. The shadows inside queue at the ticket booth, and the one behind the counter takes money and gives nothing.

The house shows one film, advertised at the booth as *Song on Fire*. Its closing credits bill Helena Ashcroft as the Spark, [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn Leatherhide]] as the Kindling, Elara Vance as the Antenna, and [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]] as the Outer God. The Spark is the name of the man who leads [[Org/Pyrelight/index|Pyrelight]] in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Teller's Run/index|Teller's Run]].

Shades in the audience can carry a caught sound. Taking the sound back out of the theater's speaker closes it again and leaves it as derelict as before.
